From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:30:04 +0000
Subject: fix(ohos): hash network cache file names and complete fetches on
 access errors

KRNetworkCacheUtil named cache files after the whole url with punctuation
replaced, with no length limit. A signed image url easily exceeds NAME_MAX,
so fs.access failed with 13900030 (File name too long); and because that
branch reported through handleLoadFailure before any callback had been
registered in downloadTasks, the FetchFileByDownloadOrCache caller was never
answered and the image stayed on its placeholder (mobile 1.13.0 11300008,
raft.7 HAR 05774fd4).

Name cache files <sha256(url)>.<ext>: the complete url participates, so two
signed urls for the same object stay distinct, and the name is fixed-length.
Bound the extension to a short alphanumeric token. On an fs.access error
complete the request with callback(null) directly.

tools/ohos-renderer-tests/check-network-cache-file-name.py locks the three
invariants (digest name, bounded extension, access-error callback) with a
mutation self-test.

Upstream-Status: pending
Fork-Patch: ohos-network-cache-hashed-file-names
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

